      "gap": "Not every Fisher 1922 estimation/information argument in the held source extent is reconstructed as an estimate or theorem with explicit model, sampling and regularity scope: (a) Section 10, pp. 342-355 (efficiency of the method of moments for the general Pearsonian system: Types I, II, IV, VII, the beta1-beta2 efficiency regions of Fig. 2 and the p. 355 efficiency tables for location/scale/form) is absent; (b) Section 11, pp. 355-356 (why moments are efficient near the normal curve: the quartic-exponent family for which moments are maximum likelihood and its agreement with the Pearson curves near the normal point) is absent; (c) the Type III large-p approximations on pp. 335-337, including the claim that efficiencies over 80 per cent occur only when p exceeds 38.1 (beta1 < 0.102, p. 336) and the large-p end-point probable-error multiplier on p. 337, are expressly not reconstructed (owned body lines 656-658); (d) the sampling calibration of Fisher's discrepancy L and of Pearson chi-square with fitted cell probabilities (pp. 357-358) is expressly not answered (owned body lines 959-962); (e) the fixed-grid periodic remainder of grouped normal information is bounded only at order a^3 (thm:p15-w02b-p15-057-grouped-phase), which the text states does not decide the a^8 terms of thm:p15-fg-expansion or Fisher's small-bin claim at a fixed phase (owned body lines 950-957; fisher-grouping lines 350-368).",
